From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:38:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vs995: drop the libwifi-hal-ctrl prebuilt, the platform
 builds it now

Soong refuses the tree:

  vendor/lge/msm8996-common/Android.bp: module "libwifi-hal-ctrl" found in multiple
      namespaces (hardware/qcom-caf/wlan/qcwcn and vendor/lge/msm8996-common)
      when including in system partition

On 22.2 only the blob provided it: the platform's copies lived in hardware/qcom/wlan/legacy and
wcn6740, neither of which this device pulls in. For 24.0 upstream added libwifi-hal-ctrl to
hardware/qcom-caf/wlan/qcwcn, which is the wlan tree msm8996 does use, so the same name now comes from
two namespaces at once.

Removing the prebuilt rather than the platform module: the platform builds it from source against the
headers it also ships (libwifi-hal-ctrl_headers), and a 2017 vendor .so is the copy to lose when the two
disagree.
---
 Android.bp | 21 ---------------------
 1 file changed, 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index a63254a..8cce851 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -1758,27 +1758,6 @@ cc_prebuilt_library_shared {
 	soc_specific: true,
 }
 
-cc_prebuilt_library_shared {
-	name: "libwifi-hal-ctrl",
-	owner: "lge",
-	strip: {
-		none: true,
-	},
-	target: {
-		android_arm: {
-			srcs: ["proprietary/vendor/lib/libwifi-hal-ctrl.so"],
-			shared_libs: ["libc++", "libc", "libm", "libdl", ],
-		},
-		android_arm64: {
-			srcs: ["proprietary/vendor/lib64/libwifi-hal-ctrl.so"],
-			shared_libs: ["libc++", "libc", "libm", "libdl", ],
-		},
-	},
-	compile_multilib: "both",
-	prefer: true,
-	soc_specific: true,
-}
-
 cc_prebuilt_library_shared {
 	name: "libxml",
 	owner: "lge",
